-- name    : mme_more_asymmetry_rational_global_entropy_data
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @marwahaha
-- created : 2026-09-07T04:28:42.731419+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/3d3ddbe2-e2f6-468b-b59f-3f3c394d11c3
-- title:
--   Exact rational global-stage entropy witness data for the 2.37134 bound
-- statement:
--   Let $D=\{(i,j,k)\in\{0,\ldots,8\}^3:i+j+k=8\}$, ordered first by $i$ and then by $j$. This definition records six explicit rational global-stage distributions $\alpha_r$, six positive reference vectors $y_r$, and additive dual potentials
--
--   $$g_r(i,j,k)=\lambda_{0,r}+\lambda_{X,r}(i)+\lambda_{Y,r}(j)+\lambda_{Z,r}(k).$$
--
--   The constants are a rationalized candidate derived from the released fourth-power numerical witness, not the original floating-point vector. Each independent probability vector is rounded to denominator $10^{15}$ after normalizing the floating-point vector, with the rounding discrepancy added to a largest coordinate; scalar potentials are rounded on the same grid. The definition also records rational allowances $\varepsilon_r$ and entropy bounds $U_r$, together with dyadic logarithm scales $k_{r,a}$ and parameters
--
--   $$t_{r,a}=\frac{2^{k_{r,a}}y_r(a)-1}{2^{k_{r,a}}y_r(a)+1},\qquad L_{r,a}=g_r(a)-\varepsilon_r.$$
--
--   These are explicit data for subsequent finite certificates of $L_{r,a}\le\log y_r(a)$ and maximum entropy at the marginals of $\alpha_r$. This definition asserts no feasibility, logarithm inequality, entropy inequality, tensor extraction, or exponent bound; those require separate proofs. Region order is $XYZ,XZY,YXZ,YZX,ZXY,ZYX$.
-- source:
--   Alman et al., More Asymmetry Yields Faster Matrix Multiplication, https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16349v2, global-stage parameters in Proposition 5.1 and Theorem 5.3, pp. 18–20, and numerical Section 7. Released code https://osf.io/mw5ak/, code_matrix_mult.zip SHA256 a88d211df0a82f0bba0a77ccbad9103064ebef08eea95613e5926a4f666260d8, member data/W1.00_2.371339.mat SHA256 783353fda82acb3fb93c247dcad857b2db5f61944f5d0e91ae5f9e5a6c7feec3. The exact rational constants here are a derived formalization candidate, not a claim that the published floating-point witness is exactly feasible.

